      "Crusade Relic§Shades of Ruin": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Antiquity Relic"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time an enemy unit within 18\" of the bearer makes an attack that targets the bearer, until the end of the phase, that enemy unit's ranged weapons have the **[HAZARDOUS]** ability.",
        "stats": {
          "Crusade Pts": {
            "value": 2
          }
        }
      },
      "Crusade Relic§Craahdekh's Throne of Sacrifice": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Antiquity Relic"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time the bearer is selected to shoot or fight, it can use this Crusade Relic. If it does, it suffers D6 mortal wounds and until the end of the phase, each time it makes an attack, you can re-roll the Wound roll.",
        "stats": {
          "Crusade Pts": {
            "value": 2
          }
        }
      },
      "Crusade Relic§Balestorm's Eye": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Legendary Relic"
          ]
        },
        "text": "The bearer always benefits from every Dread ability, regardless of which ones are currently active for your army.",
        "stats": {
          "Crusade Pts": {
            "value": 3
          }
        }
      },
      "Crusade Relic§Harbinger's Chains": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Artificer Relic"
          ]
        },
        "text": "While an enemy unit is within Engagement Range of the bearer, subtract 1 from the Objective Control characteristic of models in that enemy unit (to a minimum of 1)."
      },
      "Crusade Relic§Tyrant's Raiment": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Artificer Relic"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time the bearer makes an attack that targets a unit within range of an objective marker, add 1 to the Hit roll."
      },
      "Crusade Relic§Icon of Damnation": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Artificer Relic"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Once per battle, in your Command phase, the bearer can use this Crusade Relic. If it does, it regains up to D6 lost wounds."
      },
      "Battle Scar§Tattered Panoply": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "notWarDog"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time this model moves through a terrain feature, when rolling to see if it is Battle-shocked as a result of the Super-heavy Walker ability, it becomes Battle-shocked on a roll of 1-3."
      },
      "Battle Scar§Crippled Actuators": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Chaos Knights"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Subtract 2\" from the Move characteristic of this model and you cannot re-roll Advance rolls made for it."
      },
      "Battle Scar§Feral Machine Spirit": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Chaos Knights"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Each time you target this model with a Stratagem, roll one D6: on a 1-2, that Stratagem has no effect."
      },
      "Battle Scar§Miasmal Emissions": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "Chaos Knights"
          ]
        },
        "text": "This model cannot have the Benefit of Cover."
      },
      "Battle Scar§Inadequate Offerings": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "notWarDog"
          ]
        },
        "text": "Re-roll this result if this model has no Idolators' Offerings. In your Command phase, roll one D6: on a 1-2, randomly select one Idolators' Offering this model has. Until the start of your next Command phase, that Idolators' Offering has no effect on this model."
      },
      "Battle Scar§Faltering Reactor": {
        "keywords": {
          "Tags": [
            "notWarDog"
          ]
        },
        "text": "The range of this model's Aura abilities is reduced to a maximum of 6\" and cannot be increased by any means."
      },
      "Requisition§Vile Reworking": {
        "stats": {
          "RP": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "Purchase this Requisition at any time. You cannot use this Requisition if your Crusade force’s Idolator Influence standing level is Distrustful or Hostile. Select one CHAOS KNIGHTS TITANIC model from your Crusade force with one or more Idolators’ Offerings. Select one of those Idolators’ Offerings and remove it. You can then select a new Idolators’ Offering for that model. Afterwards, if your Idolator Influence standing level is Wary or worse, roll one D6: on a 1, your model gains a Battle Scar."
      },
      "Requisition§Path to Damnation": {
        "stats": {
          "RP": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "Purchase this Requisition after winning a battle. You cannot purchase this Requisition if your Crusade force’s Dark Gods standing level is Distrustful or Hostile. Select one CHAOS KNIGHTS TITANIC model from your Crusade army to attempt to make a pact with the Dark Gods. If that model already has a Pact of Damnation, it must break it. Remove that pact’s Dark Boon, then roll one D6: on a 4+ remove that pact’s Cursed Price; otherwise, that pact’s Cursed Price is then treated as a normal Battle Scar. Finally, roll one D6, and consult the table below to see if your model successfully gains a Pact of Damnation.\n\nDark Gods\n\nStanding Level\n\nSuccessful Result\n\n+\n\n+\n\n+"
      },
      "Requisition§Dark Ambition": {
        "stats": {
          "RP": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "Purchase this Requisition after a battle, and no more than once after each battle. Select one Power Base, and reduce your standing level with that Power Base to Hostile. For each level of standing lost when reducing it in this way, select a different Power Base and increase your standing level with that Power Base by 1.\n\nFor example, if your standing level with the Power Base you select is Aligned Interests, then you lose 4 levels of standing, and can increase your standing level with a different Power Base 4 times."
      },
      "Requisition§A New Steed": {
        "stats": {
          "RP": {
            "value": 1
          }
        },
        "text": "Purchase this Requisition at any time. Select one CHAOS KNIGHTS TITANIC unit from your Order of Battle. Remove that unit from your Order of Battle and replace it with one CHAOS KNIGHTS TITANIC unit. You cannot purchase this Requisition if doing so would cause you to exceed your Crusade force’s Supply Limit. The new unit starts with the same XP, Battle Honours, Battle Scars, Crusade points and Pacts of Damnation (if applicable) as the unit it replaced."
      },
      "Crusade Badge§Dread Baron": {
        "text": "You have the maximum standing level in at least one Power Base.\nYou have won two or more battles."
      },
      "Crusade Badge§Exalted Fiend": {
        "text": "You have the maximum standing level in at least two different Power Bases at the same time.\nYou have won six or more battles.\nAt least one CHARACTER unit from your Order of Battle has reached the Heroic rank."
      },
      "Crusade Badge§Heretic Monarch": {
        "text": "You have the maximum standing level in all three Power Bases at the same time.\nYou have won ten or more battles.\nAt least one CHARACTER unit from your Order of Battle has reached the Legendary rank.\nAdvance Moves\nWhen a unit Advances, make an Advance roll for that unit by rolling one D6. Add the result in inches to the Move characteristic of each model in that unit until the end of the phase. Each model in that unit can then make an Advance move by moving a distance in inches less than or equal to this total, but no model can be moved within Engagement Range of enemy models. A unit cannot shoot or declare a charge in the same turn that it Advanced.\nAdvance Move: Models move up to M+D6\".\nCannot move within Engagement Range of any enemy models.\nUnits that Advance cannot shoot or charge this turn.\nCharging with a Unit\nOnce you have selected an eligible unit to declare a charge, you must select one or more enemy units within 12\" of it as the targets of that charge. The targets of a charge do not need to be visible to the charging unit.\nYou then make a Charge roll for the charging unit by rolling 2D6. The result is the maximum number of inches each model in that unit can be moved if a Charge move is possible. For a Charge move to be possible, the Charge roll must be sufficient to enable the charging unit to end that move:\nWithin Engagement Range of every unit that you selected as a target of the charge.\nWithout moving within Engagement Range of any enemy units that were not a target of the charge.\nIn Unit Coherency.\nIf any of these conditions cannot be met, the charge fails and no models in the charging unit move this phase. Otherwise, the charge is successful and the models in the charging unit make a Charge move – move each model a distance in inches up to the result of the Charge roll. When doing so, each model in the charging unit must end its Charge move closer to one of the units selected as a target of its charge. If you can also move a charging model so that it ends its Charge move in base-to-base contact with one or more enemy models while still enabling the charging unit to end its move satisfying all of the conditions above, you must do so. The controlling player chooses the order in which to move their models.\nCharge Roll: 2D6\".\nTargets of a charge must be within 12\" but do not need to be visible.\nIf the distance rolled is insufficient to move within Engagement Range of all targets while maintaining Unit Coherency, the charge fails.\nCannot move within Engagement Range of any unit that was not a target of the charge.\nIf the charge is successful, each model makes a Charge move less than or equal to the Charge roll, and must move into base-to-base contact with an enemy model if possible.\nFall Back Moves\nWhen a unit Falls Back, each model in that unit can make a Fall Back move by moving a distance in inches less than or equal to its Move characteristic, and when doing so you can move it within Engagement Range of enemy models, provided it does not end that move within Engagement Range of any enemy models – if this is not possible, that unit cannot Fall Back.\nA unit cannot shoot or declare a charge in the same turn that it Fell Back."
      },
      "Amassing Power§Amassing Power": {
        "text": "**Amassing Power.** Pick your Allegiance; it sets the starting standing of your three Power Bases (Iconoclast House: Dark Gods Hostile, Idolator Influence Wary, War Dog Domination Distrustful; Infernal House: Dark Gods Wary, Idolator Influence Hostile, War Dog Domination Wary; Dreadblades: Dark Gods Distrustful, Idolator Influence Distrustful, War Dog Domination Hostile). Standing runs Hostile → Distrustful → Wary → Cautious Alliance → Aligned Interests and never leaves that range. Each time you win a battle, raise one Power Base by 1 and roll a D6 for each other base: on a 1–2 it drops by 1. Each draw or loss: roll a D6, on a 1–3 a random base drops by 1. Agendas can raise standings too; Dark Ambition (1RP) drops one base to Hostile and spreads the lost levels over the others.\n\n**Idolators’ Offerings** (Battle Traits for CHAOS KNIGHTS TITANIC models, one per suit location: Legs, Arms, Torso, Head) need Idolator Influence at Wary or better; the fourth of each location needs Cautious Alliance, the fifth needs Aligned Interests and only one model in your Order of Battle can have it. Vile Reworking (1RP) swaps one; at Wary or worse roll a D6 afterwards, on a 1 the model gains a Battle Scar.\n\n**Hunting Packs:** War Dog models take Hunt Tactics (Battle Traits) from War Dog Domination at Wary or better. At the start of the first battle round form your WAR DOG models into Hunting Packs of 2 models (2–3 at Aligned Interests); each pack picks one Hunt Tactic that its models have while within 12\" of another pack member, and becomes Ascendant once a pack member destroys an enemy unit.\n\n**Pacts of Damnation:** the Path to Damnation Requisition (1RP, after a win, not at Hostile or Distrustful) lets a TITANIC model attempt a pact; success on a D6 of 6+ at Wary, 4+ at Cautious Alliance, 2+ at Aligned Interests. A pact is one Dark Boon (Minor from Wary, Major only at Aligned Interests; no two models share a boon) plus a Cursed Price: a randomly generated Chaos Knights Battle Scar that stays until the pact is broken. One pact per model."
      },
